! Mudlet ~ a spirit's handoff, held unedited

''Register: Testimony-Verbatim.'' Nothing below makes this house's own claim. It holds what a tasked Fable spirit reported from a web-research pass, kept whole, as a ''collision surface'' rather than a briefing. The spirit read the web and four sibling reports; it read no repository code beyond one package description, and it booted nothing.

''The operator's frame it answers'' (Telarus, 2026-10-16): the Lararium rides as a ''capability added to any setup'' ~ any game, world or experience ~ with the Islands of Myth MUD as the worked example: a player's lararium and, under wizard approval, AI characters as live co-players coordinated through it as squads. Live 3D games (Katamari Damacy) stand deferred until the sensorium finishes; this survey stays on TiddlyWiki integration.

''Rulings it reads under:'' three layers held apart ~ the CRDT store as virtual backend, the TW5 VM engine, the render projections; the TW5 syncer refused as web-2.5 design; mutation-log and DOM-delta streams refused; the Web3-only law.

''Read it against us, not for us.'' Every source line names how the spirit reached it (fetched, search passage, or unreached); the Islands of Myth match and its GMCP support stand inferred. Collide it; do not inherit it.

